  Question
   The system admin team at xFusionCorp Industries has streamlined access management by implementing group-based access control. Here's what you need to do:
a. Create a group named nautilus_sftp_users across all App servers within the Stratos Datacenter.
b. Add the user rajesh into the nautilus_sftp_users group on all App servers. If the user doesn't exist, create it as well.
Note: You can find the infrastructure details by clicking on the Details of all Users and Servers button on the top-right section of the page.

         Solution
1-Login into each app server
   ssh user@host-ip
2-Create the group
   sudo groupadd nautilus_sftp_user
*If the group already exists, this will return an error you can safely ignore.
3-Ensure the user exist
Check if the user rajesh exists:
    id rajesh
*If the user does not exist, create it:
    sudo useradd rajesh
4-Add user to group
Add rajest to thr nautilus_sftp_user group
    sudo usermod -aG nautilus_sftp_users rajesh
5-Verify Membership
Confirm that  is part of the group:
    groups rajesh
You should see  listed.
6-Repeat across all apps servers
Perform the same steps on each App server in the Stratos Datacenter.
If you have Ansible or another automation tool available, you can streamline this by pushing the commands to all servers at once.
